{"id": "EUVD-2026-76991", "enisaUuid": "6317ce9a-7bc4-398f-a34c-11bcadab3078", "description": "Spug through 3.4.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability in the ping_check function that interpolates user-supplied monitor addresses directly into shell commands without validation. Authenticated users with monitor permissions can inject shell metacharacters via the /monitor/run_test/ endpoint to execute arbitrary commands as the Spug process user.", "datePublished": "2026-09-13T10:45:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:21:51", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/openspug/spug/issues/741", "https://github.com/openspug/spug", "https://github.com/openspug/spug/blob/v3.4.0/spug_api/apps/monitor/executors.py", "https://github.com/openspug/spug/blob/v3.4.0/spug_api/apps/monitor/views.py", "https://github.com/openspug/spug/commit/97aebf133e1f9cbb35ccebadab1faedfdfe93f42", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/spug-through-3.4.0-remote-code-execution-via-ping-check"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h5c4-vc34-6jcv", "CVE-2026-90770"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e9bfb223-74a7-3e45-b158-2eee92f1a18d", "product": {"name": "spug", "vendor": {"name": "openspug"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.4.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e9effd33-c15d-3c24-965b-3dc4791cec1f", "vendor": {"name": "openspug"}}], "isExploited": false}